{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_actorsystem", "label": "ActorSystem", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One per logical application. It owns the dispatcher, scheduler, supervisor tree, event stream and any registered extensions; create() returns synchronously with the root guardians spawned eagerly."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_actorsystemoptions", "label": "ActorSystemOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Constructor settings always win over anything in config \u2014 they are the explicit code-level overrides."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_guardianhierarchy", "label": "Guardian hierarchy (/user, /system, /deadLetters)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On termination the guardians go in sequence rather than together: /user drains fully first, which is what lets a user actor postStop still reach the framework actors it depends on instead of racing them into dead letters."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_extensions", "label": "Extensions (lazy plugin system)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Extensions do not initialize until reached for, which keeps single-process apps small \u2014 you adopt a feature by reaching for it and drop it by not reaching."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_terminate", "label": "system.terminate() ordered shutdown", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Notify the cluster, drain /user transitively, stop /user recursively, stop /system, close dispatcher and scheduler. Throttled and supervisor-suspended mailboxes, everything under /system, and work not yet in a mailbox are deliberately not waited for."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_shutdowndraintimeout", "label": "shutdown-drain-timeout", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returns the instant the tree goes quiet, so an idle system pays a tick rather than the budget; set to 0 to skip draining, and anything still queued when it runs out is dead-lettered."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_rununtilterminated", "label": "runUntilTerminated()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Installs signal handlers, runs the coordinated-shutdown pipeline and detaches the handlers on the way out. It holds the event loop open itself, because a Node signal handle is unreffed and would otherwise let a headless service exit before the SIGTERM it just armed for could arrive."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_deadletters", "label": "/deadLetters", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each dead letter is published on the event stream and that is all that happens by default \u2014 nothing logs them and nothing keeps them, so with no subscriber the message is gone."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_systemsperprocess", "label": "How many ActorSystems per process", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One is the common answer; a second means a separate cluster, dispatcher and supervisor tree. Worker-thread isolation and per-test fixtures are the two cases that justify it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_terminatedeadlock", "label": "Do not call terminate from inside an actor", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The mailbox cannot advance until onReceive returns, and terminate waits for the actor to stop \u2014 so awaiting it inside a handler self-deadlocks."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_guardianhierarchy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_paths_systempaths", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_actorsystem", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_actorsystemoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/actor-system.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_actorsystem", "target": "docs_src_content_d